[ f(2) = 8c - 15. \\]\n\nWe know from the problem statement that \\( f(2) = 9 \\). So we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[ 8c - 15 = 9. \\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\( c \\). First, add 15 to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[ 8c = 24. \\]\n\nThen, divide both sides by 8:\n\n\\[ c = 3. \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( c \\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{3}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:226"}
